> Is the model fitted in the right way?

Yes

> I need to parametrize ‘theta’?

Then set parameterization = "theta" in your cfa() call

> how can I interpret the coefficient (e.g A1 on g)? via the identity function?

No, it is a probit link.  But you can use the latent-response interpretation:
a 1-unit increase in "g" is associated with a {factor loading}-unit change in the expected value of the latent propensity for responding 1 to "A1".

> If I add a binary measured outcome (Y) in this way:
>
> model <- '
>
> g =~ A1 + A2+A3+ A4 + A5+A6+A7+A8+ A9+A10+ A11+A12+A13+A14+ A15
>
> Y~ g+X1
>
> '
>
> The interpretation of coefficient refers on Y is via probit?

Yes.

