Thank you so much for the explanation. I attached our hypothesized model based on theories.

 SEM-Page-4.png <https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N0KyBR4rjEcraWA1jkzuQrx_mzUQclMj/view?usp=drive_web>

The code for my baseline model is as below, I covered all variables and paths in the baseline model.

baseline_model<-
  '
  # measurement
  V =~v1 + v2 + v3 + v4
  C =~ c1 + c2 + c3 + c4

  # regressions
  H ~ age + sex
  V ~   H + age + gender
  C ~   H + age + gender + V
  R ~   H + age + gender + V + C + H
  E ~   H + age + gender + V + C + H

  #residual variance
  c1~~ c2
  c1~~ c3
  c1~~ c4
  c2 ~~ c3
  c2 ~~ c4
  c3 ~~ c4
  v1~~ v2
  v1~~ v3
  v1~~ v4
  v2 ~~ v3
  v2 ~~ v4
  v3 ~~ v4
  E~~R
  Age ~~ Gender
  '
  Would you mind checking the baseline model I drafted, I'd appreciate your help.

